{"release":{"id":395313787,"tag":"v.202610.post2","author":"sw005320","name":"v.202610.post2","draft":false,"prerelease":false,"createdAt":"2026-09-24T02:29:38Z","publishedAt":"2026-09-24T04:25:40Z","markdown":"# Summary\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n\r\nA patch on top of 202610.post1, and **nothing about installing or upgrading changes**. What changes is that the six things ESPnet does for you outside a training script have one name each and reach you four ways: `espnet transcribe`, `translate`, `phonemize`, `align`, `synthesize` and `enhance` at a terminal, the same six as MCP tools an assistant can call, a notebook each, and a Space each. Two of those are new — `espnet phonemize` reads the phones in a recording with [POWSM](https://huggingface.co/espnet/powsm_ctc), and `espnet align` lines text up with the audio it was said in, on the CTC head of any model — and they arrive with two new Spaces, [powsm-ctc](https://huggingface.co/spaces/espnet/powsm-ctc) and [forced-alignment](https://huggingface.co/spaces/espnet/forced-alignment). Every demo is now built from a directory in this repository, and the two OWSM Spaces stopped carrying their own copy of the demo page: they import the one `espnet demo` serves, which reads its menus, its window and its tasks off the checkpoint, and 746 lines of app became 166. Alignment likewise has one implementation, and the `ctc_segmentation` algorithm that was written twice is written once, in `espnet2.bin.ctc_segment`. Older checkpoints load again: a model published before June 2025 names an initialization this version removed, which no longer stops it. [`doc/front_ends.md`](https://github.com/espnet/espnet/blob/master/doc/front_ends.md) is how the seventh task gets all four front ends, and the table of what runs where is in the README, checked against the code rather than remembered.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Requirements — nothing to do\r\n\r\n| | 202610.post1 | 202610.post2 |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Python | `>=3.12,<3.14` | unchanged |\r\n| PyTorch | 2.11.0, 2.13.0, 2.14.0 | unchanged |\r\n| `pip install espnet` | inference only; training is `espnet[train]` | unchanged |\r\n\r\nA patch release, so upgrading is `pip install -U espnet` and nothing else.\r\n\r\n`espnet demo` and the Spaces need `pip install espnet[demo]` for gradio, and the MCP server `pip install espnet[mcp]` — neither is a dependency, because no inference path should need a web framework or a protocol server to import.\r\n\r\n## Important PRs\r\n\r\n### New Features\r\n\r\n- **PR #6750**: [Audio metrics 03/12] Add metric tokenization and constrained ARECHO search (by @ftshijt)\r\n\r\n### Recipe\r\n\r\n- **PR #6793**: A Space for forced alignment (by @sw005320)\r\n- **PR #6792**: A Space for POWSM-CTC, and its four tasks in the browser (by @sw005320)\r\n- **PR #6787**: One CTC segmentation, not two — and one naming for the alignment modules (by @sw005320)\r\n- **PR #6780**: MCP: translate, phonemize and align, under the names the CLI uses (by @sw005320)\r\n- **PR #6779**: One name a task: `espnet transcribe` and `espnet synthesize` (by @sw005320)\r\n- **PR #6763**: [espnet3] readme -> README in recipe (by @Masao-Someki)\r\n- **PR #6761**: Follow espnet/notebook's flat Demos layout (by @sw005320)\r\n- **PR #6738**: [espnet3] Bugfix for espnet3.parallel, local environment (by @Masao-Someki)\r\n\r\n### Bugfix\r\n\r\n- **PR #6796**: The doc build dies on a page it will not name (by @sw005320)\r\n- **PR #6790**: Two ways an alignment goes wrong quietly (by @sw005320)\r\n- **PR #6782**: An initialization this version removed must not stop a model loading (by @sw005320)\r\n- **PR #6764**: [espnet3] Bugfix - freezing model parameters (by @Masao-Someki)\r\n\r\n### Documentation\r\n\r\n- **PR #6794**: One page, and one specification for the six tasks (by @sw005320)\r\n- **PR #6778**: Say which tasks run where (by @sw005320)\r\n- **PR #6777**: One alignment, on torchaudio's forced alignment (by @sw005320)\r\n- **PR #6776**: The demo page is the checkpoint's, not OWSM's (by @sw005320)\r\n- **PR #6775**: Add `espnet phonemize`: the phones in a recording, with POWSM (by @sw005320)\r\n- **PR #6768**: Say which demos are checked, where people click them (by @sw005320)\r\n- **PR #6749**: [Audio metrics 02/12] Add Uni-VERSA regression with checkpoint-compatible parameters (by @ftshijt)\r\n- **PR #6747**: Support structured annotations and missing references (by @ftshijt)\r\n\r\n### CI\r\n\r\n- **PR #6798**: A Space that is not uploaded yet is not a broken link (by @sw005320)\r\n- **PR #6765**: Wait a rate limit out rather than call the demo links broken (by @sw005320)\r\n\r\n### Release\r\n\r\n- **PR #6791**: Bump the version to 202610.post2 (by @sw005320)","html":"<div class=\"markdown-heading\"><h1 class=\"heading-element\">Summary</h1><a id=\"user-content-summary\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Summary\" href=\"#summary\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\"></span></a></div>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\">Overview</h2><a id=\"user-content-overview\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Overview\" href=\"#overview\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\"></span></a></div>\n<p>A patch on top of 202610.post1, and <strong>nothing about installing or upgrading changes</strong>. What changes is that the six things ESPnet does for you outside a training script have one name each and reach you four ways: <code>espnet transcribe</code>, <code>translate</code>, <code>phonemize</code>, <code>align</code>, <code>synthesize</code> and <code>enhance</code> at a terminal, the same six as MCP tools an assistant can call, a notebook each, and a Space each. Two of those are new — <code>espnet phonemize</code> reads the phones in a recording with <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/espnet/powsm_ctc\" rel=\"nofollow\">POWSM</a>, and <code>espnet align</code> lines text up with the audio it was said in, on the CTC head of any model — and they arrive with two new Spaces, <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/spaces/espnet/powsm-ctc\" rel=\"nofollow\">powsm-ctc</a> and <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/spaces/espnet/forced-alignment\" rel=\"nofollow\">forced-alignment</a>. Every demo is now built from a directory in this repository, and the two OWSM Spaces stopped carrying their own copy of the demo page: they import the one <code>espnet demo</code> serves, which reads its menus, its window and its tasks off the checkpoint, and 746 lines of app became 166. Alignment likewise has one implementation, and the <code>ctc_segmentation</code> algorithm that was written twice is written once, in <code>espnet2.bin.ctc_segment</code>. Older checkpoints load again: a model published before June 2025 names an initialization this version removed, which no longer stops it. <a href=\"https://github.com/espnet/espnet/blob/master/doc/front_ends.md\"><code>doc/front_ends.md</code></a> is how the seventh task gets all four front ends, and the table of what runs where is in the README, checked against the code rather than remembered.</p>\n<hr>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\">Requirements — nothing to do</h2><a id=\"user-content-requirements--nothing-to-do\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Requirements — nothing to do\" href=\"#requirements--nothing-to-do\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\"></span></a></div>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>202610.post1</th>\n<th>202610.post2</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Python</td>\n<td><code>&gt;=3.12,&lt;3.14</code></td>\n<td>unchanged</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>PyTorch</td>\n<td>2.11.0, 2.13.0, 2.14.0</td>\n<td>unchanged</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>pip install espnet</code></td>\n<td>inference only; training is <code>espnet[train]</code>\n</td>\n<td>unchanged</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>A patch release, so upgrading is <code>pip install -U espnet</code> and nothing else.</p>\n<p><code>espnet demo</code> and the Spaces need <code>pip install espnet[demo]</code> for gradio, and the MCP server <code>pip install espnet[mcp]</code> — neither is a dependency, because no inference path should need a web framework or a protocol server to import.</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\">Important PRs</h2><a id=\"user-content-important-prs\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Important PRs\" href=\"#important-prs\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\"></span></a></div>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\"><h3 class=\"heading-element\">New Features</h3><a id=\"user-content-new-features\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: New Features\" href=\"#new-features\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\"></span></a></div>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<strong>PR #6750</strong>: [Audio metrics 03/12] Add metric tokenization and constrained ARECHO search (by @ftshijt)</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\"><h3 class=\"heading-element\">Recipe</h3><a id=\"user-content-recipe\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Recipe\" href=\"#recipe\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\"></span></a></div>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<strong>PR #6793</strong>: A Space for forced alignment (by @sw005320)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>PR #6792</strong>: A Space for POWSM-CTC, and its four tasks in the browser (by @sw005320)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>PR #6787</strong>: One CTC segmentation, not two — and one naming for the alignment modules (by @sw005320)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>PR #6780</strong>: MCP: translate, phonemize and align, under the names the CLI uses (by @sw005320)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>PR #6779</strong>: One name a task: <code>espnet transcribe</code> and <code>espnet synthesize</code> (by @sw005320)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>PR #6763</strong>: [espnet3] readme -&gt; README in recipe (by @Masao-Someki)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>PR #6761</strong>: Follow espnet/notebook's flat Demos layout (by @sw005320)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>PR #6738</strong>: [espnet3] Bugfix for espnet3.parallel, local environment (by @Masao-Someki)</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\"><h3 class=\"heading-element\">Bugfix</h3><a id=\"user-content-bugfix\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Bugfix\" href=\"#bugfix\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\"></span></a></div>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<strong>PR #6796</strong>: The doc build dies on a page it will not name (by @sw005320)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>PR #6790</strong>: Two ways an alignment goes wrong quietly (by @sw005320)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>PR #6782</strong>: An initialization this version removed must not stop a model loading (by @sw005320)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>PR #6764</strong>: [espnet3] Bugfix - freezing model parameters (by @Masao-Someki)</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\"><h3 class=\"heading-element\">Documentation</h3><a id=\"user-content-documentation\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Documentation\" href=\"#documentation\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\"></span></a></div>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<strong>PR #6794</strong>: One page, and one specification for the six tasks (by @sw005320)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>PR #6778</strong>: Say which tasks run where (by @sw005320)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>PR #6777</strong>: One alignment, on torchaudio's forced alignment (by @sw005320)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>PR #6776</strong>: The demo page is the checkpoint's, not OWSM's (by @sw005320)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>PR #6775</strong>: Add <code>espnet phonemize</code>: the phones in a recording, with POWSM (by @sw005320)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>PR #6768</strong>: Say which demos are checked, where people click them (by @sw005320)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>PR #6749</strong>: [Audio metrics 02/12] Add Uni-VERSA regression with checkpoint-compatible parameters (by @ftshijt)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>PR #6747</strong>: Support structured annotations and missing references (by @ftshijt)</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\"><h3 class=\"heading-element\">CI</h3><a id=\"user-content-ci\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: CI\" href=\"#ci\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\"></span></a></div>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<strong>PR #6798</strong>: A Space that is not uploaded yet is not a broken link (by @sw005320)</li>\n<li>\n<strong>PR #6765</strong>: Wait a rate limit out rather than call the demo links broken (by @sw005320)</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\"><h3 class=\"heading-element\">Release</h3><a id=\"user-content-release\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Release\" href=\"#release\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\"></span></a></div>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<strong>PR #6791</strong>: Bump the version to 202610.post2 (by @sw005320)</li>\n</ul>\n","assets":[]}}